  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vijay S/O Piniya Poojari vs The State Of Karnataka on 20 November, 2024 Author: Pradeep Singh Yerur Bench: Pradeep Singh Yerur -1- Nc: 2024:Khc-D:16994 Wp No. 106364 of 2024 In The High Court Of Karnataka, Dharwad Bench Dated This The 20Th Day Of November, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Pradeep Singh Yerur Writ Petition No. 106364 Of 2024 (Gm-Police) Between: 1. Vijay S/O Piniya Poojari Age 48 Years, Occ Business, Owner Of Hotel Shri Panjurli, Opp Hubli Scan Centre, Deshpande Nagar, Hubballi, Dist Dharwad 58001. 2. Chandrasekhar S/O Kalu Shetty Age 54 Years, Occ Business, R/O House No. 100, Shembagi Layout, Kotilingeshwar Nagar, Gokul Road, Mallikarjun Rudrayya Hubballi, Dist Dharwad 580001. Kalmath Location: High 3 . Shreekar S/O Nandyappa Shetty Court Of Karnataka Age 40 Years, Occ Business, Dharwad Bench R/O House No. 100, Shembagi Layout, Vijay S/O Piniya Poojari vs The State Of Karnataka on 20 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/173969996/ 1 Kotilingeshwar Nagar, Gokul Road, Hubballi, Dist Dharwad 580001. ...Petitioners (By Sri.V M Sheelvant, Advocate) And: 1. The State Of Karnataka Rep By Its Secretary, -2- Nc: 2024:Khc-D:16994 Wp No. 106364 of 2024 Department Of Home, Vidhahna Soudha, Bangalore 560001. 2. Commissioner Of Police, Hubli-Dharwad, Dharwad District, Dharwad 580001. 3. Circle Police Inspector, Hubli Sub-Urban Police Station, Hubballi 580023. 4. Circle Police Inspector, Old Hubli Police Station, Hubballi 580023. ...Respondents (By Sri.V.S.Kalasurmath, Aga) This Wp Is Filed Under Articles 226 & 227 Of The Constitution Of India, Praying To (1) Issue A Writ In The Nature Of Mandamus Or Any Other Appropriate Writ, Order OR DIRECTIONS DECLARING THAT THE RESPONDENTS HAVE NO AUTHORITY TO RESTRICT THE BUSINESS HOURS OF THE PETITIONERS VIZ., HOTEL SHRI PANJURLI, HOTEL VINAYAK VEG AND NON VEG AND SHREE CHINESE FAST FOOD CENTER AT OLD HUBLI TILL 11 P.M. ONLY IN THE INTEREST OF JUSTICE AND EQUITY. (II) ISSUE A WRIT OR ANY OTHER APPROPRIATE ORDER OR DIRECTION RESTRAINING THE RESPONDENTS FROM INTERFERING WITH DAY TODAY BUSINESS OF THE PETITIONERS VIZ., HOTEL SHRI PANJURLI, HOTEL VINAYAK VEG AND NON VEG AND SHREE CHINESE FAST FOOD CENTER AT OLD HUBLI, IN THE INTEREST OF JUSTICE AND EQUITY & (III) GRANT SUCH OTHER RELIEF'S AS THIS HON'BLE COURT DEEMS FIT IN Vijay S/O Piniya Poojari vs The State Of Karnataka on 20 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/173969996/ 2 CIRCUMSTANCES OF THE CASE. THIS PETITION, COMING ON FOR PRELIMINARY HEARING 'B' GROUP, THIS DAY, THE COURT MADE THE FOLLOWING: -3- NC: 2024:KHC-D:16994 WP No. 106364 of 2024 CORAM: THE HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE PRADEEP SINGH YERUR ORAL ORDER (PER: THE HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE PRADEEP SINGH YERUR)",
    "facts": "The establishments of the petitioners are registered under the Food Safety and Security Act, 2006 and have obtained GSTIN number, as required. ii. A writ of mandamus is issued directing the respondent-authorities not to restrict the business hours of the petitioners namely Hotel Shri Panjurli, Hotel Vinayak Veg & Non-Veg and Shree Chinese Fast Food Centre at Old Hubballi in accordance with the Rules and Regulations NC: 2024:KHC-D:16994 more so as per the official memorandum dated 19.09.2024, which permits till 1.00 a.m. Sd/- (PRADEEP SINGH YERUR) JUDGE KGK Vijay S/O Piniya Poojari vs The State Of Karnataka on 20 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/173969996/ 5",
    "arguments": "5. It is the grievance of the petitioners that respondent Nos.3 and 4-authorities and its officials are acting without any authority of law and there being no rules, regulations or enactment to shut down or close the business and running of the hotel/restaurant at 10.00 or 11.00 p.m. are unauthorizedly and illegally, with ill-motive and malafide intention, threatening the petitioners to close down their business at 11.00 p.m."
  },
